WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:04.074
Transforming how we lead together:

2
00:00:04.074 --> 00:00:08.020
a handbook for moving from hierarchies towards co-creation.

3
00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:13.646
Public organisations are under enormous pressure.

4
00:00:13.646 --> 00:00:18.722
Climate change, AI, an ageing population, loneliness and burnout.

5
00:00:18.722 --> 00:00:24.189
These challenges are complex and connected, and can't be solved inside

6
00:00:24.189 --> 00:00:25.360
one department.

7
00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:31.310
Many organisations say they want self-leadership and trust-based

8
00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:32.023
leadership.

9
00:00:32.023 --> 00:00:34.163
But as one public servant put it:

10
00:00:34.163 --> 00:00:37.340
I have never experienced any of that in practice.

11
00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:44.015
This handbook grew out of four years of participatory research with

12
00:00:44.015 --> 00:00:48.745
Swedish municipalities and agencies, exploring leadership through

13
00:00:48.745 --> 00:00:52.020
choreography, photography, poetry and design.

14
00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:55.270
Its central idea:

15
00:00:55.270 --> 00:00:59.022
real change happens on three levels at once.

16
00:00:59.022 --> 00:01:01.153
The I, our inner beliefs.

17
00:01:01.153 --> 00:01:04.394
The we, our relationships and culture.

18
00:01:04.394 --> 00:01:07.890
And the it, our structures and processes.

19
00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:14.255
Six chapters move from why we need to change, through self-leadership,

20
00:01:14.255 --> 00:01:18.819
culture and new roles, to participatory structures, and designing your

21
00:01:18.819 --> 00:01:20.580
own transformation journey.

22
00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:26.675
Along the way are tried and tested practices, from the core quadrant

23
00:01:26.675 --> 00:01:31.034
and dialogue, to consent-based decisions and movement scores for your

24
00:01:31.034 --> 00:01:31.350
team.

25
00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:37.219
You'll hear voices from the field, and follow Elena, a fictional

26
00:01:37.219 --> 00:01:41.479
manager in elderly care, trying to lead differently inside a system

27
00:01:41.479 --> 00:01:42.560
full of barriers.

28
00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:48.888
Here you can search the whole handbook, browse the practice library,

29
00:01:48.888 --> 00:01:52.950
time a movement score, and keep a private reflection journal.

30
00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:57.580
Leading together isn't a destination.

31
00:01:57.580 --> 00:01:58.804
It's a practice.

32
00:01:58.804 --> 00:02:00.563
Start wherever you are.

33
00:02:00.563 --> 00:02:01.940
You are not alone.

